{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:normal-space","title":"def:normal-space","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":330,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:normal-space","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:normal-space","line":553,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The Normal Space]\n\\label{def:normal-space}\n\n\\uses{lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian}\n\n\n\nFor an immersion $F:M^n\\to\\widetilde M^m$, identify $T_xM$ with $\\operatorname{im}dF_x\\subseteq T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M$. The normal space is\n\\[\nN_xM=\\{v\\in T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M:\\widetilde g_{F(x)}(v,w)=0\\text{ for every }w\\in T_xM\\}.\n\\]\nIt is a linear subspace, and $T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M=T_xM\\oplus N_xM$ orthogonally.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The Normal Space] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6e6f726d616c2d7370616365\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian\">↗ lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian</a> <p></p>For an immersion <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F:M^n\\to \\widetilde M^m$\">$F:M^n\\to \\widetilde M^m$</span>, identify <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_xM$\">$T_xM$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {im}dF_x\\subseteq T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M$\">$\\operatorname {im}dF_x\\subseteq T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M$</span>. The normal space is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  N_xM=\\{ v\\in T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M:\\widetilde g_{F(x)}(v,w)=0\\text{ for every }w\\in T_xM\\} .  \\]\">\\[  N_xM=\\{ v\\in T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M:\\widetilde g_{F(x)}(v,w)=0\\text{ for every }w\\in T_xM\\} .  \\]</span> It is a linear subspace, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M=T_xM\\oplus N_xM$\">$T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M=T_xM\\oplus N_xM$</span> orthogonally. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames-immersed","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","title":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","label":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","label":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:normal-bundle","title":"prop:normal-bundle","label":"prop:normal-bundle"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal","title":"def:unit-normal","label":"def:unit-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal","title":"lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal","label":"lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-unit-normal-field","title":"def:smooth-unit-normal-field","label":"def:smooth-unit-normal-field"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:normal-space","title":"def:normal-space","tex":"\\begin{definition}[The Normal Space]\n\\label{def:normal-space}\n\n\\uses{lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian}\n\n\n\nFor an immersion $F:M^n\\to\\widetilde M^m$, identify $T_xM$ with $\\operatorname{im}dF_x\\subseteq T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M$. The normal space is\n\\[\nN_xM=\\{v\\in T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M:\\widetilde g_{F(x)}(v,w)=0\\text{ for every }w\\in T_xM\\}.\n\\]\nIt is a linear subspace, and $T_{F(x)}\\widetilde M=T_xM\\oplus N_xM$ orthogonally.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","title":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}